# escape_gate_sidh -- the gate to the hollow hills (north-east): a fairy thorn grown through it, and a session going
# full tilt on the far side. What it shows, and why it is shut.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 5

= the thorn
@continue
A hawthorn has grown up here through the stone, gnarled as an old man’s knuckle,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
blossom on it white as milk, blooming in this dark. Its trunk is hollow where a door should be.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= the session
@continue
And from behind it, a session in full cry: fiddles racing each other,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
feet stamping the floor, a roar of laughter, a voice lifting into a song.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
You stand out in the cold, like one outside a lit house on a winter’s night.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= where it goes
Beyond are the hollow hills, the bright halls of the sídh. The latch is on their side.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
And no one cuts a fairy thorn: not a champion, not a king with all his host behind him,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
not if he values his cattle, his children, his luck, his mind.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
